# Components

## Layout

- **File naming:** PascalCase (`EventCard.tsx`, `AdminEventForm.tsx`).
- **One main export per file**, named the same as the file.
- **Co-locate tests** in `components/<domain>/__tests__/<Name>.test.tsx`.

## Folders by domain

- `components/ui/` — shadcn-style primitives (Button, Input, Form, Select, Dialog, …)
- `components/admin/` — admin-only forms and panels
- `components/auth/` — login/register/forgot/reset
- `components/events/` — event card, list, details, form
- `components/layout/` — header, navigation, shell
- `components/profile/` — profile editor
- `components/registration/` — event registration flow
- `components/legal/` — legal content
- `components/shared/` — cross-domain widgets
- `components/providers/` — provider wrapper components (QueryProvider, etc.)

## `"use client"` discipline

- **Default = server component.** Only add `"use client"` when the file needs hooks, browser APIs, event handlers, or React context.
- For mostly-static pages with one interactive bit, extract the interactive bit into its own client component and import it from the server page.

## Props

- Type props with an `interface <Name>Props { … }` defined just above the component.
- Pull shared types from `types/<domain>.ts` — don't redefine them inline.
- For polymorphic primitives (`Button`, similar), support `asChild` via `@radix-ui/react-slot` and use the CVA + `cn()` pattern.

## Class merging

- Always merge classNames with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`. Never string-concat them.

## Design tokens

- Use token utilities or CSS vars from the unified design system: `bg-brand`, `text-on-brand`, `text-ink`, `bg-surface`, `border-line`, `var(--brand)`, `var(--ink)`, etc.
- Never hardcode colors, use `hsl(var(--...))`, revive `--gr-*`, or add `.gr-dark` / `.gr-light`.
- Green is action/accent only. Do not use brand green for body text or links, and never put white text on bright `bg-brand`; use `text-on-brand`.
- For new UI: prefer the GoRun variant set (`brand`, `primary`, `soft`, `ghost-gr`). Legacy shadcn variants (`default`, `secondary`, …) are kept for back-compat only.

## i18n

- All user-visible text goes through `useTranslations("<scope>")`. Add keys to BOTH `messages/en.json` AND `messages/uk.json` in the same edit.

## Reference

- Canonical primitive: `components/ui/button.tsx`
- Canonical complex form: `components/admin/AdminEventForm.tsx`
- Canonical context+hook: `hooks/useAuth.tsx`
